{"task_id": "HumanEval/11", "solution": "```python\ndef string_xor(a: str, b: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Performs binary XOR operation on two input strings of '0's and '1's.\n    Pads shorter strings with leading zeros to match length before XORing.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not all(c in '01' for c in a) or not all(c in '01' for c in b):\n        raise ValueError(\"Input strings must only contain '0' or '1' characters.\")\n\n    max_len = max(len(a), len(b))\n    a_padded = a.zfill(max_len)\n    b_padded = b.zfill(max_len)\n\n    result_bits = []\n    for i in range(max_len):\n        bit_a = int(a_padded[i])\n        bit_b = int(b_padded[i])\n        result_bits.append(str(bit_a ^ bit_b))\n\n    return \"\".join(result_bits)\n```"}
