{"task_id": "HumanEval/19", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List\n\n\ndef sort_numbers(numbers: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Input is a space-delimited string of numberals from 'zero' to 'nine'.\n    Valid choices are 'zero', 'one', 'two', 'three', 'four', 'five', 'six', 'seven', 'eight' and 'nine'.\n    Return the string with numbers sorted from smallest to largest\n    >>> sort_numbers('three one five')\n    'one three five'\n    \"\"\"\n\n    # Custom exception for invalid number words as per design.\n    class InvalidNumberWordError(ValueError):\n        def __init__(self, word: str):\n            self.word = word\n            super().__init__(f\"'{word}' is not a valid number word (0-9).\")\n\n    # In-memory mapping of number words to integers as per design.\n    _NUMBER_WORD_MAP = {\n        \"zero\": 0, \"one\": 1, \"two\": 2, \"three\": 3, \"four\": 4,\n        \"five\": 5, \"six\": 6, \"seven\": 7, \"eight\": 8, \"nine\": 9\n    }\n    _INT_TO_WORD_MAP = {v: k for k, v in _NUMBER_WORD_MAP.items()}\n\n    # Helper for converting a number word to its integer value.\n    def _word_to_int_local(word: str) -> int:\n        if word not in _NUMBER_WORD_MAP:\n            raise InvalidNumberWordError(word)\n        return _NUMBER_WORD_MAP[word]\n\n    # Helper for converting an integer back to its number word.\n    def _int_to_word_local(num: int) -> str:\n        if num not in _INT_TO_WORD_MAP:\n            raise ValueError(f\"'{num}' is not a valid integer for number word conversion (0-9).\")\n        return _INT_TO_WORD_MAP[num]\n\n    # FR1: Validate input type.\n    if not isinstance(numbers, str):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input 'numbers' must be a string.\")\n\n    # Handle empty or purely whitespace inputs.\n    if not numbers.strip():\n        return \"\"\n\n    # FR2: Parse the input string into individual number words.\n    word_list: List[str] = numbers.split()\n    \n    int_list: List[int] = []\n    # FR3: Convert each number word to its corresponding integer value.\n    for word in word_list:\n        int_list.append(_word_to_int_local(word))\n    \n    # FR4: Sort the integer values in ascending order.\n    int_list.sort()\n    \n    sorted_word_list: List[str] = []\n    # FR5: Convert the sorted integer values back to their corresponding number words.\n    for num in int_list:\n        sorted_word_list.append(_int_to_word_local(num))\n            \n    # FR6: Return a space-delimited string of the sorted number words.\n    return \" \".join(sorted_word_list)\n```"}
