{"task_id": "HumanEval/36", "solution": "```python\ndef count_digit_in_number(num: int, digit: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts occurrences of a specific digit within a number.\n    It converts the number to a string and uses string count.\n    \"\"\"\n    return str(num).count(str(digit))\n\n\ndef fizz_buzz(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Return the number of times the digit 7 appears in integers less than n\n    which are divisible by 11 or 13. Raises ValueError for non-positive integer input.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(n, int) or n <= 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input 'n' must be a positive integer.\")\n\n    total_sevens_count = 0\n    for i in range(1, n):\n        # Check if the number is divisible by 11 or 13.\n        if (i % 11 == 0) or (i % 13 == 0):\n            total_sevens_count += count_digit_in_number(i, 7)\n\n    return total_sevens_count\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/35", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import Union\n\nclass InvalidInputError(ValueError):\n    \"\"\"Exception raised for invalid input types.\n    It indicates that the provided input is not a Python list.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message: str = \"Input must be a list.\"):\n        super().__init__(message)\n\nclass EmptyListError(ValueError):\n    \"\"\"Exception raised when an empty list is provided.\n    This signifies that no maximum element can be determined.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message: str = \"Input list cannot be empty.\"):\n        super().__init__(message)\n\nclass InvalidElementError(TypeError):\n    \"\"\"Exception raised when a list contains non-comparable elements.\n    This prevents the comparison operation from successfully completing.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message: str = \"List contains non-comparable elements.\"):\n        super().__init__(message)\n\ndef max_element(l: list) -> Union[int, float]:\n    \"\"\"Return maximum element in the list.\n    This function handles input validation and raises specific errors for invalid cases.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(l, list):\n        raise InvalidInputError()\n\n    if not l:\n        raise EmptyListError()\n\n    max_val = l[0]\n    try:\n        for element in l[1:]:\n            if element > max_val:\n                max_val = element\n    except TypeError:\n        raise InvalidElementError()\n\n    return max_val\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/36", "solution": "```python\ndef fizz_buzz(n: int):\n    \"\"\"Return the number of times the digit 7 appears in integers less than n which are divisible by 11 or 13.\n    >>> fizz_buzz(50)\n    0\n    >>> fizz_buzz(78)\n    2\n    >>> fizz_buzz(79)\n    3\n    \"\"\"\n    # Define a helper function to count digit occurrences within a number.\n    # This delegates the task, aligning with the design's utility class concept.\n    def _count_digit_in_number(num: int, digit: int) -> int:\n        return str(num).count(str(digit))\n\n    # Validate input 'n' to ensure it is a positive integer.\n    # This fulfills FR1's error handling and precondition requirements.\n    if not isinstance(n, int):\n        raise ValueError(\"Input 'n' must be an integer.\")\n    if n <= 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input 'n' must be a positive integer.\")\n\n    total_sevens = 0\n    # Iterate through numbers from 1 up to n-1, as specified by FR2 and business rules.\n    # For each number, check divisibility by 11 or 13.\n    for i in range(1, n):\n        if i % 11 == 0 or i % 13 == 0:\n            # If divisible, count the occurrences of digit 7 in the number.\n            # This implements FR4 and accumulates the result for FR5.\n            total_sevens += _count_digit_in_number(i, 7)\n\n    return total_sevens\n```"}
