{"task_id": "HumanEval/39", "solution": "```python\nclass PrimeFibCalculator:\n    \"\"\"Manages generation of Fibonacci numbers and primality testing.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.prime_cache = {}\n\n    def is_prime(self, num: int) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Determines if a given integer is a prime number, using a cache.\"\"\"\n        if num in self.prime_cache:\n            return self.prime_cache[num]\n        if num < 2:\n            self.prime_cache[num] = False\n            return False\n        for i in range(2, int(num**0.5) + 1):\n            if num % i == 0:\n                self.prime_cache[num] = False\n                return False\n        self.prime_cache[num] = True\n        return True\n\n    def find_nth_prime_fib(self, n: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Calculates and returns the N-th number that is both Fibonacci and prime.\"\"\"\n        if n < 1:\n            raise ValueError(\"n must be a positive integer.\")\n\n        prime_fib_count = 0\n        a, b = 0, 1  # F(0) and F(1) of the Fibonacci sequence.\n\n        fib_sequence_iterations = 0\n        while True:\n            c = a + b  # Generate the next Fibonacci number.\n            a, b = b, c  # Update the sequence terms for the next iteration.\n\n            fib_sequence_iterations += 1\n\n            if c > 1 and self.is_prime(c):\n                prime_fib_count += 1\n                if prime_fib_count == n:\n                    return c\n\n            # Prevents indefinite loops for extreme N if the sequence somehow doesn't yield N primes quickly.\n            if fib_sequence_iterations > 100000:\n                raise RuntimeError(\"Exceeded maximum Fibonacci generation limit without finding n-th prime fib.\")\n\ndef prime_fib(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"prime_fib returns n-th number that is a Fibonacci number and it's also prime.\"\"\"\n    calculator = PrimeFibCalculator()\n    return calculator.find_nth_prime_fib(n)\n```"}
