{"task_id": "HumanEval/44", "solution": "```python\ndef change_base(x: int, base: int) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Converts an integer x from base 10 to its string representation in the specified base.\n    The target base must be an integer between 2 and 9 (inclusive).\n    \"\"\"\n    # Validate input number x.\n    if not isinstance(x, int):\n        raise ValueError(\"Number x must be an integer.\")\n    if x < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Number x must be a non-negative integer.\")\n\n    # Validate target base.\n    if not isinstance(base, int):\n        raise ValueError(\"Base must be an integer.\")\n    if not (1 < base < 10):\n        raise ValueError(\"Base must be an integer between 2 and 9 (inclusive).\")\n\n    if x == 0:\n        return \"0\"\n\n    result_digits = []\n    # Perform base conversion using repeated division and remainder collection.\n    while x > 0:\n        remainder = x % base\n        result_digits.append(str(remainder))\n        x //= base\n    \n    # Construct the string representation from collected remainders.\n    return \"\".join(reversed(result_digits))\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/43", "solution": "```python\ndef pairs_sum_to_zero(l):\n    \"\"\"\n    pairs_sum_to_zero takes a list of integers as an input.\n    it returns True if there are two distinct elements in the list that\n    sum to zero, and False otherwise.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(l, list):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input must be a list.\")\n    if not all(isinstance(n, int) for n in l):\n        raise TypeError(\"All elements in the list must be integers.\")\n\n    if len(l) < 2:\n        return False\n\n    seen_numbers = set()\n    for num in l:\n        complement = -num\n        if complement in seen_numbers:\n            return True\n        seen_numbers.add(num)\n    return False\n```"}
