{"task_id": "HumanEval/46", "solution": "```python\ndef fib4(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Computes the n-th element of the Fib4 sequence iteratively.\n    Raises ValueError for negative input n.\"\"\"\n    if n < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input 'n' must be a non-negative integer.\")\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    if n == 1:\n        return 0\n    if n == 2:\n        return 2\n    if n == 3:\n        return 0\n\n    # Initialize the first four values of the sequence.\n    fib_sequence = [0, 0, 2, 0] \n\n    # Compute subsequent values iteratively up to n.\n    for i in range(4, n + 1):\n        next_fib = fib_sequence[i-1] + fib_sequence[i-2] + fib_sequence[i-3] + fib_sequence[i-4]\n        fib_sequence.append(next_fib)\n    \n    return fib_sequence[n]\n```"}
