{"task_id": "HumanEval/59", "solution": "```python\ndef largest_prime_factor(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the largest prime factor of a given integer n.\n    Assumes n > 1 and n is not a prime number.\n    \"\"\"\n    largest_factor = 1\n    i = 2\n    temp_n = n\n\n    # Divide by 2 until n is odd.\n    while temp_n % 2 == 0:\n        largest_factor = 2\n        temp_n //= 2\n\n    # Iterate for odd factors; check up to sqrt(temp_n).\n    while i * i <= temp_n:\n        while temp_n % i == 0:\n            largest_factor = i\n            temp_n //= i\n        i += 2 # Only check odd numbers.\n\n    # If temp_n is still greater than 2, it is the largest prime factor remaining.\n    if temp_n > 2:\n        largest_factor = temp_n\n\n    return largest_factor\n```"}
