{"task_id": "HumanEval/79", "solution": "```python\ndef decimal_to_binary(decimal):\n    \"\"\"Converts a decimal integer to its binary string representation, prefixed and suffixed with 'db'.\n    This function handles both positive and negative integers as specified.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Ensure input is an integer as required by FR1.\n    if not isinstance(decimal, int):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input 'decimal' must be an integer.\")\n\n    # Handle zero as a special case, returning \"db0db\".\n    if decimal == 0:\n        return \"db0db\"\n\n    is_negative = decimal < 0\n    abs_decimal = abs(decimal)\n\n    # Convert absolute decimal to binary string, removing '0b' prefix.\n    binary_str = bin(abs_decimal)[2:]\n\n    # Apply 'db' prefix/suffix and handle negative sign (FR2, FR3, FR6).\n    if is_negative:\n        return f\"-db{binary_str}db\"\n    else:\n        return f\"db{binary_str}db\"\n```"}
