{"task_id": "HumanEval/91", "solution": "import re\n\ndef is_bored(S):\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts the number of sentences that start with the word \"I\".\n    Sentences are delimited by '.', '?' or '!'.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(S, str):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input must be a string.\")\n\n    boredom_count = 0\n    \n    # Define sentence delimiters as specified.\n    SENTENCE_DELIMITERS = ['.', '?', '!'] \n\n    # Replace delimiters with a unique marker to reliably split sentences.\n    text_with_markers = S\n    for delimiter in SENTENCE_DELIMITERS:\n        text_with_markers = text_with_markers.replace(delimiter, delimiter + \"|SENTENCE_END|\")\n    \n    # Split the text by the marker, trim whitespace, and filter out empty segments.\n    sentences = [s.strip() for s in text_with_markers.split(\"|SENTENCE_END|\") if s.strip()]\n\n    for sentence in sentences:\n        cleaned_sentence = sentence.strip()\n        # Use regex to check if the sentence starts with the standalone word \"I\", case-insensitive.\n        if re.match(r\"^I\\b\", cleaned_sentence, re.IGNORECASE) is not None:\n            boredom_count += 1\n            \n    return boredom_count"}
