{"task_id": "HumanEval/99", "solution": "```python\nimport math\n\ndef closest_integer(value: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Converts a string to a number and returns the closest integer.\n    Equidistant numbers (X.5) are rounded away from zero.\n    \"\"\"\n    num = float(value)\n\n    # Calculate floor and ceiling integers\n    rounded_down = math.floor(num)\n    rounded_up = math.ceil(num)\n\n    # Calculate distances to the floor and ceiling integers\n    diff_down = abs(num - rounded_down)\n    diff_up = abs(num - rounded_up)\n\n    if diff_down < diff_up:\n        return int(rounded_down)\n    elif diff_up < diff_down:\n        return int(rounded_up)\n    else:  # Equidistant, e.g., X.5\n        if num >= 0:\n            return int(rounded_up)  # Round up for positive numbers.\n        else:\n            return int(rounded_down) # Round down for negative numbers.\n```"}
