{"task_id": "HumanEval/103", "solution": "```python\nimport math\n\ndef rounded_avg(n, m):\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the rounded average of integers in a range and returns its binary string.\n    Returns -1 if n is greater than m.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n > m:\n        return -1\n\n    count = m - n + 1\n    # Calculate sum using the arithmetic series formula for efficiency.\n    sum_val = (count * (n + m)) // 2\n\n    average = sum_val / count\n\n    # Round to the nearest integer, with 0.5 rounding up, as specified.\n    rounded_avg_val = int(math.floor(average + 0.5))\n\n    return bin(rounded_avg_val)\n```"}
