{"task_id": "HumanEval/150", "solution": "```python\nimport math\n\ndef x_or_y(n, x, y):\n    \"\"\"A simple program which should return the value of x if n is\n    a prime number and should return the value of y otherwise.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def _is_prime_checker(number: int) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Checks if the input integer is a prime number. It raises TypeError for non-integer inputs.\"\"\"\n        if not isinstance(number, int):\n            raise TypeError(\"n must be an integer\")\n        if number <= 1:\n            return False\n        if number == 2:\n            return True\n        if number % 2 == 0:\n            return False\n        # Iterate from 3 up to sqrt(n) (inclusive), incrementing by 2.\n        for i in range(3, int(math.sqrt(number)) + 1, 2):\n            if number % i == 0:\n                return False\n        return True\n\n    if _is_prime_checker(n):\n        return x\n    else:\n        return y\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/151", "solution": "```python\ndef double_the_difference(lst):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of squares of odd, strictly positive integers in the input list.\n    Non-integers, negative numbers, and zero are ignored; returns 0 for an empty list.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not lst:\n        return 0\n\n    total_sum_of_squares = 0\n    for num in lst:\n        # Filter for numbers that are integers, positive, and odd.\n        if isinstance(num, int) and num > 0 and num % 2 != 0:\n            total_sum_of_squares += num * num\n            \n    return total_sum_of_squares\n```"}
