{"task_id": "HumanEval/152", "solution": "```python\nclass InvalidInputError(ValueError):\n    \"\"\"Custom exception for invalid input specifically within the comparison logic.\n    It inherits from ValueError to signify issues with the value of an argument.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message: str):\n        self.message = message\n        super().__init__(self.message)\n\ndef compare(game, guess):\n    \"\"\"Compares actual game scores against guessed scores and returns a list of absolute differences.\n    Raises InvalidInputError for invalid input types, lengths, or non-integer elements.\"\"\"\n\n    # Validate input types for lists as per FR1.\n    if not isinstance(game, list) or not isinstance(guess, list):\n        raise InvalidInputError(\"Input 'game' and 'guess' must be lists.\")\n\n    # Validate input lengths as per FR1.\n    if len(game) != len(guess):\n        raise InvalidInputError(\"Input arrays 'game' and 'guess' must be of equal length.\")\n\n    differences = []\n    # Calculate the absolute difference for each corresponding element as per FR2, BR1, BR2.\n    for i in range(len(game)):\n        # Validate element types as per FR1.\n        if not isinstance(game[i], int) or not isinstance(guess[i], int):\n            raise InvalidInputError(\"All elements in 'game' and 'guess' must be integers.\")\n        \n        differences.append(abs(game[i] - guess[i]))\n    \n    # Return the new array of differences as per FR3.\n    return differences\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/152", "solution": "```python\ndef compare(game: list[int], guess: list[int]) -> list[int]:\n    \"\"\"Compares actual game scores against guessed scores, returning the absolute difference for each match.\n    A difference of 0 indicates a perfectly correct guess.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(game) != len(guess):\n        raise ValueError(\"Input arrays 'game' and 'guess' must be of equal length.\")\n\n    differences = []\n    for i in range(len(game)):\n        game_score = game[i]\n        guess_score = guess[i]\n\n        if not isinstance(game_score, int) or not isinstance(guess_score, int):\n            raise TypeError(\"All elements in 'game' and 'guess' arrays must be integers.\")\n\n        if game_score == guess_score:\n            differences.append(0)\n        else:\n            differences.append(abs(game_score - guess_score))\n            \n    return differences\n```"}
