{"task_id": "HumanEval/153", "solution": "```python\nclass Extension:\n    \"\"\"A data transfer object (DTO) to hold an extension's name and its calculated strength.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, name: str, strength: int):\n        if not isinstance(name, str):\n            raise TypeError(\"Extension name must be a string.\")\n        if not isinstance(strength, int):\n            raise TypeError(\"Extension strength must be an integer.\")\n        self.name = name\n        self.strength = strength\n\n    def __repr__(self) -> str:\n        return f\"Extension(name='{self.name}', strength={self.strength})\"\n\n\nclass ExtensionStrengthCalculator:\n    \"\"\"Encapsulates the logic for calculating the strength of a single extension string.\"\"\"\n    def calculate(self, extension_name: str) -> int:\n        if not isinstance(extension_name, str):\n            raise TypeError(\"Extension name for strength calculation must be a string.\")\n\n        cap_count = sum(1 for char in extension_name if 'A' <= char <= 'Z')\n        sm_count = sum(1 for char in extension_name if 'a' <= char <= 'z')\n        return cap_count - sm_count\n\n\nclass StrongestExtensionFinder:\n    \"\"\"Contains the core business logic for iterating through a list of Extension objects and identifying the one with the highest strength.\"\"\"\n    def find_strongest(self, extensions: list[Extension]) -> Extension:\n        if not extensions:\n            raise ValueError(\"The list of extensions cannot be empty.\")\n\n        strongest_extension_obj = extensions[0]\n        max_strength = strongest_extension_obj.strength\n\n        for ext_obj in extensions[1:]:\n            if ext_obj.strength > max_strength:\n                max_strength = ext_obj.strength\n                strongest_extension_obj = ext_obj\n        \n        return strongest_extension_obj\n\n\ndef Strongest_Extension(class_name: str, extensions: list[str]) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Finds the strongest extension for a given class name based on character casing strength.\n    Returns a formatted string \"ClassName.StrongestExtensionName\".\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(class_name, str):\n        raise TypeError(\"Class name must be a string.\")\n    if not isinstance(extensions, list):\n        raise TypeError(\"Extensions must be a list.\")\n    \n    calculator = ExtensionStrengthCalculator()\n    finder = StrongestExtensionFinder()\n\n    processed_extensions = []\n    for ext_name in extensions:\n        strength = calculator.calculate(ext_name)\n        processed_extensions.append(Extension(name=ext_name, strength=strength))\n\n    strongest_ext = finder.find_strongest(processed_extensions)\n\n    return f\"{class_name}.{strongest_ext.name}\"\n```"}
